1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,777
Easy with the table. The leg is loose
again.

2
00:00:16,632 --> 00:00:18,772
Is the shim still underneath?

3
00:00:24,264 --> 00:00:26,975
By the broom. I've been looking for it all
morning.

4
00:00:37,347 --> 00:00:41,123
I thought you wanted to take Ma's mug
home.

5
00:00:44,979 --> 00:00:49,237
Leave it by the kettle for now. The
water’s still warm.

6
00:00:52,611 --> 00:00:54,919
Did you boil it earlier?

7
00:01:05,694 --> 00:01:08,185
Yes. I still set out two cups.

8
00:01:13,326 --> 00:01:16,419
I'm still using it. There's water in the
kettle.

9
00:01:20,958 --> 00:01:25,798
The buyer says she'll be here at five. Mr.
Nestor will come first.

10
00:01:34,042 --> 00:01:35,036
What for?

11
00:01:41,674 --> 00:01:44,445
I told him he could have the table.

12
00:01:49,306 --> 00:01:52,242
Did you tell him when he could collect it?

13
00:02:02,389 --> 00:02:06,481
Before the buyer gets here. I thought it
would help.

14
00:02:10,021 --> 00:02:12,315
We’re still here. There’s time.

15
00:02:17,653 --> 00:02:19,584
I said we'd talk about it.

16
00:02:30,736 --> 00:02:33,113
I thought we had.

17
00:02:38,368 --> 00:02:41,263
You asked if it would fit in the car.
That's different.

18
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,030
I'll call and ask him to wait.

19
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,276
Mr. Nestor, can you give me a minute? I'll
call back.

20
00:03:11,632 --> 00:03:15,650
Yesterday I still had a key. I could come
back.

21
00:03:19,264 --> 00:03:23,543
Today I have to decide what to do with a
cracked saucer.

22
00:03:32,347 --> 00:03:36,731
Leave it on the rack for now. There’s room
in the box.

23
00:03:39,979 --> 00:03:43,017
I can still hear Ma saying it’s good for
another day.

24
00:03:47,611 --> 00:03:50,329
If you want the table, I'll bring it over.

25
00:04:00,694 --> 00:04:03,420
Where would I put it? My place is crowded
as it is.

26
00:04:08,326 --> 00:04:11,831
Is this where you sat when you had coffee
together?

27
00:04:15,958 --> 00:04:19,176
Ma sat there. I sat here so I could see
her at the sink.

28
00:04:29,042 --> 00:04:33,823
On the phone I could always hear her
rattling dishes.

29
00:04:36,674 --> 00:04:40,463
She’d tuck the phone against her shoulder
so she could wash up.

30
00:04:44,306 --> 00:04:47,945
I used to think she wanted to hang up.

31
00:04:57,389 --> 00:05:00,142
Let Mr. Nestor have it. Tell him about the
shim.

32
00:05:05,021 --> 00:05:08,728
Let's move it aside. It's blocking the
cupboard.

33
00:05:12,653 --> 00:05:15,102
Support the bottom. It got wet once.

34
00:05:25,736 --> 00:05:29,739
Nena. Her handwriting. She still had this
when we moved here?

35
00:05:33,368 --> 00:05:35,652
Yes. I carried it onto the jeep.

36
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,629
This towel was Auntie's.

37
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,440
Ben, stay here. Keep your feet up.

38
00:06:12,391 --> 00:06:14,401
Wait. I can see Ma.

39
00:06:20,782 --> 00:06:24,400
Hold on to me. The floor is slippery.

40
00:06:35,167 --> 00:06:36,191
Ma! I'm here!

41
00:06:43,558 --> 00:06:47,608
Cover your nose and mouth. Here, take my
towel.

42
00:06:51,949 --> 00:06:55,094
Why are we moving? She hasn't got in yet.

43
00:07:06,333 --> 00:07:08,420
Can we wait for her at the corner?

44
00:07:14,724 --> 00:07:18,114
We’re going to the school. We’ll meet her
there.

45
00:07:23,115 --> 00:07:25,132
Does she know where we’re going?

46
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:41,213
Yes. She stopped to tell me before you got
in.

47
00:07:45,891 --> 00:07:49,387
Don't lean out. Sit here.

48
00:07:54,282 --> 00:07:56,280
You still remember her towel?

49
00:08:08,667 --> 00:08:12,438
She pulled me in. I had no slippers.

50
00:08:17,058 --> 00:08:21,307
I thought you were still home. So many
people passed in front of me.

51
00:08:25,449 --> 00:08:30,031
Every time someone moved beside me, I lost
sight of her.

52
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:43,105
Ma looked at the jeep. I waved.

53
00:08:48,224 --> 00:08:52,313
Someone lifted a sack. When it came down,
she was heading home.

54
00:08:56,615 --> 00:08:58,677
You saw her look at you?

55
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,003
I thought she saw me.

56
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,558
Auntie's name is on the envelope.

57
00:09:44,549 --> 00:09:48,487
Wait. Check when she wrote it.

58
00:09:55,097 --> 00:09:57,466
We were still at the school. Here’s the
date.

59
00:10:13,181 --> 00:10:15,597
It had only been one night.

60
00:10:23,729 --> 00:10:25,572
Was she going to send it?

61
00:10:34,278 --> 00:10:36,203
I don't know. Let's open it.

62
00:10:52,361 --> 00:10:54,835
Thank you for getting Ben onto the jeep.

63
00:11:02,910 --> 00:11:06,602
I went back to the house. I thought he was
still inside.

64
00:11:13,458 --> 00:11:15,706
I thought he was still inside.

65
00:11:31,542 --> 00:11:33,531
There's more. Here, at the bottom.

66
00:11:42,090 --> 00:11:45,328
Wait. Let me read the first line again.

67
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:55,425
Hold it near the window. The ink’s faded.

68
00:12:10,722 --> 00:12:13,578
She didn’t know I’d already gotten in.

69
00:12:21,271 --> 00:12:22,937
She didn’t know yet.

70
00:12:31,819 --> 00:12:35,023
I called out to her. I thought she heard
me.

71
00:12:49,903 --> 00:12:52,494
Why did she think I was inside?

72
00:13:00,451 --> 00:13:02,500
She asked me where you were.

73
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,293
What did you say?

74
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,846
Lita, where's your brother?

75
00:13:45,088 --> 00:13:48,337
I sent him for his slippers. He might
still be inside.

76
00:13:56,175 --> 00:13:58,747
Get in. Sit next to Auntie.

77
00:14:15,182 --> 00:14:16,653
Ma, I'll wait for you.

78
00:14:26,270 --> 00:14:28,440
There’s still room here. Look.

79
00:14:37,358 --> 00:14:40,776
Give Auntie your bag. I’ll meet you at the
school.

80
00:14:56,365 --> 00:14:58,310
Get in, sweetheart. I'll follow.

81
00:15:07,453 --> 00:15:09,440
Lita, give me your hand.

82
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:20,931
When I looked, you were gone.

83
00:15:37,547 --> 00:15:43,503
I was already on the jeep. Behind the
sack.

84
00:15:48,635 --> 00:15:50,902
I saw you once we started moving.

85
00:15:59,723 --> 00:16:03,883
I raised my hand to call her. She’d
already turned away.

86
00:16:18,730 --> 00:16:23,336
All I knew was she left after I waved.

87
00:16:29,818 --> 00:16:33,177
We both waved. She didn’t see either of
us.

88
00:16:40,905 --> 00:16:43,201
Why didn't you tell me?

89
00:16:59,912 --> 00:17:03,874
I thought you remembered waking up next to
her.

90
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,005
I remember that. I remember both.

91
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,767
Ben? Can you hear me?

92
00:17:42,346 --> 00:17:46,403
I called for him in the kitchen. In the
bedroom. Even under the house.

93
00:17:50,692 --> 00:17:53,017
His slippers were by the door.

94
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,495
I put them in my pocket. He might want
them when I found him.

95
00:18:13,346 --> 00:18:18,083
I went through the kitchen again. The
light switch was still on, though the
power was out.

96
00:18:21,692 --> 00:18:25,305
Outside, a neighbor told me the jeep had
already gone.

97
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,737
That’s when I thought you might have made
it aboard.

98
00:18:44,346 --> 00:18:46,776
Nena. Here he is. He finally fell asleep.

99
00:18:52,692 --> 00:18:54,031
Is he hurt?

100
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,987
No. He was just looking for you.

101
00:19:15,346 --> 00:19:16,017
Ma?

102
00:19:23,692 --> 00:19:24,899
I'm here, sweetheart.

103
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,442
The towel is cold.

104
00:19:46,346 --> 00:19:48,102
Hold my hand.

105
00:19:54,692 --> 00:19:56,332
Do you have my slippers?

106
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,197
Yes, in my pocket. You can put them on
tomorrow.

107
00:20:17,346 --> 00:20:18,561
Stay here for a while.

108
00:20:25,692 --> 00:20:26,909
I’m right here.

109
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,105
Her hand was warm. That's what I remember.

110
00:20:48,346 --> 00:20:51,506
The whole ride, I kept waiting for her to
turn around.

111
00:20:56,692 --> 00:21:01,253
We got there together. You didn't speak to
me until that night.

112
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,443
I didn't know how to ask.

113
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,056
How many times did you think it was your
fault?

114
00:21:42,391 --> 00:21:45,360
When it rains hard, I still think about
it.

115
00:21:50,782 --> 00:21:53,892
I said you might still be inside. Might.
That's all I said.

116
00:22:05,167 --> 00:22:07,201
That's all you knew then.

117
00:22:13,558 --> 00:22:16,477
If I’d gotten off before the jeep started
moving…

118
00:22:21,949 --> 00:22:24,554
Then she would’ve gone looking for both of
us.

119
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:39,074
I’ve wanted to tell you for so long.

120
00:22:44,724 --> 00:22:46,451
I hear you now.

121
00:22:53,115 --> 00:22:54,512
Want some coffee?

122
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:10,556
Yeah. Is there any sugar left?

123
00:23:15,891 --> 00:23:19,310
In the tin. Ma only put one spoonful in
yours.

124
00:23:24,282 --> 00:23:25,821
You still remember that?

125
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:43,822
You're the one who forgets. You used to
ask for two.

126
00:23:47,058 --> 00:23:48,846
Here. You get the mug.

127
00:23:55,449 --> 00:23:59,711
The coffee won’t drink itself if we just
keep looking at it.

128
00:24:09,833 --> 00:24:12,714
There’s still time. Let’s sit a little
longer.

129
00:24:18,224 --> 00:24:20,320
So that's where the saucer went.

130
00:24:26,615 --> 00:24:28,627
I needed something to set it on.

131
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:41,945
Still hot.

132
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,909
Sorry. I think I'm early.

133
00:25:11,063 --> 00:25:14,164
That's fine. Let me show you the back
door.

134
00:25:18,126 --> 00:25:21,913
Lift it a little, then slide the bolt.

135
00:25:30,234 --> 00:25:31,818
Like this? There. Thank you.

136
00:25:37,297 --> 00:25:39,095
Here are the keys.

137
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:46,126
Which one is for the back?

138
00:25:56,468 --> 00:26:01,136
The one with the circle. Ma marked it so
she could tell them apart.

139
00:26:03,532 --> 00:26:05,704
All right. I’ll leave the mark on.

140
00:26:10,595 --> 00:26:13,817
The mug's in the box, with the letter.

141
00:26:22,703 --> 00:26:26,085
I thought you’d take it to the car
yourself.

142
00:26:29,766 --> 00:26:31,154
I’ll wait for you.

143
00:26:36,829 --> 00:26:38,900
Keep a hand under the bottom.

144
00:26:48,937 --> 00:26:50,693
I've got it. Ready?

145
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,268
Yeah. Together.
